  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Centre for Rights Education and Awareness (CREAW) is a feminist nonprofit women&apos;s rights organization founded in 1998 with a vision of a just society where Kenyan women and girls enjoy full rights and live in dignity. Its mission is to champion, expand, and actualize women and girls&#x2019; rights and social justice. CREAW aims to scale up its interventions, expand its subnational geographical reach, and further strengthen grassroots women-led organizations&#x2019; capacities to design, own, and lead interventions that champion the rights of women and girls in Kenya.</narrative>
  </description>
